  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing (NAICS 334511) has drawn $12.1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The market delivered 7,709 awards with an average award size of $1.6M, and obligations fell 34.2% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $10B, while the Department of Transportation follows with $1.1B and the Department of Homeland Security with $851M. Yearly obligations show a peak run from FY23 to FY25 before the current-year decline: FY21 $13.2B, FY22 $13.9B, FY23 $17B, FY24 $17.1B, FY25 $18.4B, FY26 $12.1B. Vendors are concentrated among large defense primes: RAYTHEON COMPANY appears multiple times with the largest single vendor totals, and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION and NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORPORATION are also prominent. Smaller civilian agencies account for considerably less buying, with individual agency totals in the tens of millions. This snapshot covers partial fiscal-year totals and only contract obligations through the fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
